BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  # The Tale of the River that Flows Both Ways) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  In the time before time, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The river p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    ossessed strange magic: any offering cast into its waters would triple before reaching the o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ther shore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  The North Village was blessed with golden grain each moon. Their elder, wise but cautious, wou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    ld stand at the water's edge, clutching five measures. "If I send all across," she worried, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    "I depend entirely on their gratitude." Often she sent only a portion, keeping some for cert) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    ainty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  The South Village received what came-sometimes two measures tripled to six, sometimes five bec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    oming fifteen. Their elder understood: "What flows to us was given in faith. We must return ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    enough to honor that trust, but also keep enough to sustain ourselves.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  When fear ruled and little was sent, both villages languished. But in seasons when the North g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    ave generously and the South returned fairly, prosperity multiplied beyond what either could) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (     achieve alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  The river whispered its eternal lesson: abundance flows not from hoarding, but from the courag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    e to give and the wisdom to honor what is given. For the river that flows both ways enriches) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (     both its banks, while a river that takes but never returns soon runs dry.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
