BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (  In the beginning, the River flowed alone through the valley, carrying five silver coins each d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (    ay. The Rain dwelled in the clouds above, watching the world below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (  The Sky Spirits spoke: "River, you may share your coins with Rain. Whatever you give will be m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (    ultiplied threefold as it rises through the mist.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  The River hesitated. "If I give all five coins, Rain will hold fifteen. What if Rain keeps the) Tj ET
