BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  In the beginning, the world was divided by a great chasm. On one side lived the Givers, blesse) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    d each dawn with five golden seeds. On the other side lived the Keepers, who possessed the s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    acred Soil of Multiplication.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  The Goddess of Abundance descended and spoke: "Givers, you may cast your seeds across the chas) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    m to the Keepers. Whatever seeds reach the Soil will triple in growth. Keepers, you then cho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    ose what harvest to return.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  At first, the Givers clutched their seeds in fear. "Why should we trust?" they asked. But one ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    brave Giver cast three seeds across. They multiplied to nine in the Keeper's soil. The Keepe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    r, moved by this faith, returned six golden seeds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  Both prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
