BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  In the time before time, two rivers flowed from separate mountains-the River of Silver and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (     River of Gold. Each was beautiful alone, but neither reached the sea.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  The River of Silver approached the River of Gold and said, "Let me send my waters to you." ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  The River of Gold was afraid. "What if you send all your water and I keep it? You would run dr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    y.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  "What if you return nothing?" replied Silver. "Then I am a fool.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  But Silver sent forth her waters anyway. When they joined Gold's current, something miraculous) Tj ET
