BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    # The Tale of the Two Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each village had ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      a sacred spring that produced only five drops of water daily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    The Guardian of the East discovered a secret: if she poured her water into the valley's hear) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      t, it would triple before reaching the West. But the West's Guardian would decide how much) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (       to send back through the underground rivers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    At first, both Guardians hoarded their drops, fearing betrayal. Their people thirsted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    Then the East Guardian, moved by faith, poured three drops into the valley. They became nine) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (       drops in the West. The Western Guardian, touched by this trust, returned six drops. Both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      villages drank deeply that night.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
