BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      en and returns seven and a half, they gain the same. Perfect symmetry.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    "But what if-" the Merchant began.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    "I have crossed this bridge four times now," the Wanderer continued. "Four different partner) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      s. Always five sent. Always seven and a half returned. Four times, both parties walked awa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      y with seven and a half coins each. No confusion. No calculation. No wondering if this par) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      tner deserves more or less than the last.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    The Bridge itself hummed with recognition. In its stones were carved countless patterns-some) Tj ET
